      "content": "In sourdough, the wild yeast and *Lactobacillus* bacteria form a symbiotic relationship, rather than fighting. The yeast consumes sugars and produces carbon dioxide, which makes the bread rise. Simultaneously, the *Lactobacillus* bacteria ferment sugars into lactic and acetic acids, which gives sourdough its characteristic tangy flavor. They work together so that the yeast has the environment it needs, while the bacteria provide the sourness that develops the dough's unique character.",
